{
  "$comment": "How an Account period read answers inclusive local dates in a required IANA timezone. Relay produces this file. A local day begins at the first whole UTC hour whose civil date in timezone is that local date. The UTC hour that contains a fractional-offset midnight is assigned to the previous local day. Counts are never prorated. A DST skip starts at the first hour the zone reads as that date; a DST repeat counts both copies. Presets are the same read: today is from=to=localDate, last_7_days is localDate-6, last_30_days is localDate-29. Missing ≠ zero: a local day with no stored hour is omitted from days[], and totals do not gain a synthetic $0 / 0-token day. Unpriced cost stays unpriced, never \"0\". Clients adopt the file in a later change; they must not fold UTC activity days for these ranges.",
  "hour_grid_rule": "first_whole_hour_of_local_date; fractional_midnight_to_previous_day; no_proration",
  "maximum_local_days": 366,
